{"nodes": [{"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_design", "label": "RDS Full Privatization Design (2026-07-30)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_roadmap", "label": "Phase 0-9 Privatization Roadmap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordered by four principles: observe first, additive changes first, easily reversible first, and irreversible public-access removal only after 100% of consumers have migrated."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase0_observability", "label": "Phase 0 \u2014 VPC Flow Logs Observability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nobody knows which clients currently connect to RDS, so any migration without measurement is guesswork. One Flow Logs enablement answers both Q1 (read1 unknown connections) and Q3 (spd-test EIP whitelisting) and is reversible with a single delete."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase3_developer_access", "label": "Phase 3 \u2014 Developer Access Path (Hard Gate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "After Phase 7 the ms_codegen, ps_path, ps_jupyter and mysqldump workflows all die. SSM port forwarding is the default because every developer already has an IAM user and all tools are local CLIs; Client VPN's $73/month fixed cost is only justified if non-IAM users must reach the DB, and a bastion would recreate the inbound-22 problem being removed."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase5_lambda_vpc_migration", "label": "Phase 5 \u2014 Migrating 145 Lambdas Into the VPC", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Largest workload and highest risk. ms_sam only reads template.yaml, so there is no single injection point; the chosen lever makes the VPC identifier live in one SSM parameter, the logic in ms_sam, and per-repo work a mechanical codemod plus a dependency bump. A CFN Macro was rejected because the templates already carry two transforms."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase7_rds_public_disable", "label": "Phase 7 \u2014 RDS Public Access Removal (Only Downtime Window)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ENI reconfiguration plus DNS switch severs existing connections for tens of seconds to minutes. Ordered dev-mshuttle, spd-test, read1, then the protected production writer last, each at least three days apart and each gated on seven consecutive days of zero external srcaddr in Flow Logs."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_default_vpc_private_subnet_augmentation", "label": "Augment Default VPC With Private Subnets (Not a New VPC)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EFS can hold mount targets in only one VPC, so moving to a new VPC would force destructive delete-and-recreate on a protected resource; the 2017-AMI EC2 has no SSM and no documentation and is not reproducible. Adding subnets to the default VPC is purely additive and fully reversible. The 'default' attribute belongs only to the four pre-created subnets, so newly created subnets are unaffected by it."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_publicly_accessible_root_cause", "label": "Exposure Cause Is PubliclyAccessible=true, Not Public Subnets", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An ENI without a public IP is unreachable from the internet even with an IGW route, so the risky, downtime-bearing subnet-group move can be separated from the actual security win and deferred to an optional Phase 9."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_split_horizon_dns", "label": "RDS Split-Horizon DNS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because the default VPC has DNS support and hostnames enabled, an RDS FQDN resolves to a private IP inside the VPC and a public IP outside. Hardcoded host strings therefore keep working after privatization, which decouples 'replace hostnames' from 'remove plaintext passwords' and sharply reduces migration scope."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_buildtime_secret_baking", "label": "Secrets Baked Into Bundles at Build Time", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "secret.cjs reads Secrets Manager into .env.<stage> and webpack BannerPlugin inlines the values at the top of the bundle, with zero runtime Secrets Manager calls. Three consequences: rotating a secret propagates nothing without a full rebuild and redeploy, a Secrets Manager interface endpoint is unnecessary (~$19/month saved), and plaintext production credentials persist in every historical artifact in the ms-sam S3 bucket."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_ms_sam_toolchain", "label": "ms_sam Deployment Toolchain", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_stack_name_collision", "label": "Four Duplicate CloudFormation Stack Names", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same stack is deployed from two or more source locations, so adding VpcConfig to the new repo is silently reverted whenever someone deploys the old monorepo. If that happens after privatization the affected Lambda loses its database."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_nat_gateway_requirement", "label": "NAT Gateway Is Mandatory", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "34 backend repos depend on axios/@slack/webhook and call external SaaS (NHN Toast SMS, Kakao AlimTalk, Slack, FCM, OAuth, Channel.io, Notion), so private-subnet Lambdas cannot function without egress."}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_ssm_port_forwarding", "label": "SSM Port Forwarding Jump Host", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_plaintext_db_credentials", "label": "P0-1 Plaintext Production DB Credentials in Git", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_console_log_process_env", "label": "P0-2 console.log(process.env) Dumps All Secrets to CloudWatch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_ms_sam_s3_artifacts", "label": "P1-3 ms-sam S3 Bucket Artifact Secret Residue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_design", "target": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_roadmap", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_roadmap", "target": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase0_observability", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_roadmap", "target": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase3_developer_access", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_roadmap", "target": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase5_lambda_vpc_migration", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_rds_privatization_roadmap", "target": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase7_rds_public_disable", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase3_developer_access", "target": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase7_rds_public_disable", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "llm-wiki/aws-ops/2026-07-30-vpc-rds-privatization-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase0_observability", "target": "llm_wiki_aws_ops_2026_07_30_vpc_rds_privatization_design_phase7_rds_public_disable", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRA